<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk"><!--
    Core depends on nothing: no UI, no hardware, no providers. This is what makes the
    replay harness possible (architecture.md §3, §8) and it is asserted by
    CoreHasNoForbiddenDependencies in D47.Core.Tests, not just documented here.
  -->


  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.ProtectedData" Version="10.0.11" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    The shipped cue set is embedded rather than copied beside the executable. 760 KB against
    a ~50 MB publish is nothing, and it is one less loose file to keep beside the exe — the
    Whisper natives already have to live there, but nothing else should (architecture.md §9).

    They live in Core because a WAV is bytes: parsing and asserting one cue per loop state
    needs no audio device, which is what lets CueLibrary be covered by Core's tests. The
    logical names are what CueLibrary enumerates, so the shipped set *is* the table — there
    is no second list of cue names anywhere to disagree with this one (Phase 5, #20).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="..\..\assets\cues\*.wav" LogicalName="D47.Core.Cues.%(Filename)" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="..\..\assets\alerts\*.wav" LogicalName="D47.Core.Alerts.%(Filename)" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="..\..\assets\beds\*.wav" LogicalName="D47.Core.Beds.%(Filename)" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Ship and module figures, generated by tools/gen-elite-specs.py from EDCD/FDevIDs and
    EDCD/coriolis-data. 80 KB, embedded rather than loose beside the exe for the same reason
    the cues are, and read on first use rather than at startup — Phase 14 asks for a
    dataset "lazy-queried at runtime", and a Commander who never asks a specification
    question never pays to parse it.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Knowledge\EliteSpecifications.tsv" LogicalName="D47.Core.EliteSpecifications" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Knowledge\Engineers.tsv" LogicalName="D47.Core.Engineers" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Knowledge\Materials.tsv" LogicalName="D47.Core.Materials" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Knowledge\Blueprints.tsv" LogicalName="D47.Core.Blueprints" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Knowledge\OnFoot.tsv" LogicalName="D47.Core.OnFoot" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Knowledge\Lore.tsv" LogicalName="D47.Core.LoreTable" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    The capability documentation, embedded so the panel can draw the ELI5 band at the top of a
    page (asked for 2026-08-22). The published site and the in-app help are the same bytes: the
    band is authored once, in the markdown, and read a second time by HelpLibrary — so a page
    cannot say one thing in a browser and another in a headset.

    All of them rather than only the ones written so far. A page with no band parses to null and
    is simply not offered, which means adding one is an edit to the markdown and nothing else.
    ~520 KB against a ~50 MB publish, the same trade the cues above already make.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="..\..\docs\capabilities\*.md" LogicalName="D47.Core.Help.%(Filename)" />

    <!--
      The three general help pages — Overview, Installing, Talking to Directive 47 — which live a
      folder up and are not capabilities. Prefixed, because docs/conversation.md and
      docs/capabilities/conversation.md would otherwise both want the name "conversation" and one
      would silently win.
    -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="..\..\docs\*.md" LogicalName="D47.Core.Help.general-%(Filename)" />

    <!--
      The changelog, so About can show it with no internet (#50). It is not under docs/ and so
      falls into neither glob above, and it is a release list rather than a banded help article -
      so it is read as text by Core.Help.Changelog rather than parsed by HelpLibrary.

      6,000-odd lines. Compressed into a ~50 MB bundle that is not a size problem, and the
      alternative was the button that was there before: a browser, which needs a network to answer
      a question about the build already on the machine.
    -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="..\..\CHANGELOG.md" LogicalName="D47.Core.Changelog" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
